The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
sock_poll_wait(file, sock, wait);
if (pool->cached_need_wakeup) {
```
Reason:
The `sock_poll_wait` function is called unconditionally, causing the `poll()` function to sleep even when the `need_wakeup` flag is set. This prevents the driver from processing Rx and/or Tx operations promptly, leading to delays until the timeout expires.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (pool->cached_need_wakeup) {
    if (xs->zc)
        xsk_wakeup(xs, pool->cached_need_wakeup);
    else
        __xsk_sendmsg(sk);
} else {
    sock_poll_wait(file, sock, wait);
}
```
Reason:
The patch introduces a check for the `cached_need_wakeup` flag before calling `sock_poll_wait`. If the flag is set, it wakes up the driver immediately instead of sleeping, ensuring that Rx and/or Tx processing occurs promptly. Only if the flag is not set does it allow the process to sleep, adhering to the intended functionality.

